==Old English==

===Etymology===
Common Germanic, from Indo-European ''*leb-, *lob-''.  Cognate with Old Frisian ''slepa'', Old High German ''[[slāfan]]'' (German ''[[schlafen]]''), Old Saxon ''slāpan'' (Dutch ''[[slapen]]''), Gothic [[𐍃𐌻𐌴𐍀𐌰𐌽]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/'slæ:p.ɑn/|lang=ang}}

===Verb===
{{Latinx|'''slǣpan'''}} (class VII strong: {{Latinx|'''slǣpþ'''}} ‘he sleeps’; {{unicode|'''slēp'''}} ‘he slept’; {{unicode|'''slēpon'''}} ‘they slept’; {{Latinx|'''ġeslǣpen'''}} past participle)

# to [[sleep]]

